    {
      "id": "1541266589427695678",
      "type": "Default",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-24T02:03:10.268+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "I want it to be, because if you get that on this slow node, the same tricks should let us pull off PAM4 32GBaud (PCIe 6.0) on IHP SG13CMOS5L, even if not at full reach but mandating a redriver (with integrated DFE; as close as would be reasonable to route and with no connectors between the ASIC and the redriver) isn't excessive at that point...\n\nWhich I do not think is reasonable to be on the table, unless it's literally the DFE that locks these fast transports from these affordable-MPW nodes.",
      "author": {
